-- let_forward_reference at 10:13, ONCE (`language.md` §7): two values that
-- define each other are one forward reference, not two. `a = b + 1` reads `b`
-- before it has a value and is reported; `b = a` reads a binding written
-- above it, which is legal on its own and says nothing about the cycle. One
-- report per binding that runs too soon is what keeps a chain of them from
-- printing the same mistake n times.
c =
    let
        a = b + 1

        b = a
    in
    a + b
